urple glow gives something a unique look that really stands out.\n  - style: Dave commented that Calvin's unique style stands out in his music and playing. Calvin previously customized an item with a shiny finish to match his style.\n  - purple hue: Dave commented that the guitar has a gorgeous purple hue and asked why it was made so shiny.\n  - electronic elements: Calvin has been experimenting with adding electronic elements to his songs to give them a fresh vibe, as part of his process of self-discovery.\n  - the sunlight: Dave commented that the sunlight hitting Calvin's item (a sign of hard work) is lovely and a great symbol of Calvin's dedication, making Calvin proud.\n  - lights: Calvin mentioned that the lights in a photo were great, noting that they looked lively.\n  - creative haven: Calvin refers to his 'creative haven' as the place where he pours his heart into music, following a flood incident.\n  - music: Calvin and an artist discussed favorite artists, art, and music's power to connect people, leading to a creative high for Calvin. Dave also noted music fosters creativity.\n  - playing: Dave commented that Calvin's unique style really stands out in his playing.\n  - new stuff: Calvin is trying to find the right balance between sticking to his sound and trying new stuff in his music, finding it exciting and motivating.\n  - strum: Calvin mentioned that every 'mark and strum holds a story' about his performance on a big stage.\n  - beauty: Calvin is proud of his car, which he calls a \"beauty\"; it reminds him of his hard work and dedication and inspires him.\n  - mansion: Calvin threw a party for his new album at his Japanese house/mansion, following a prior event where he recorded a song there after meeting Frank Ocean.\n  - blast: Calvin mentioned that something \"sounds like a blast\" and asked which one was the favorite.\n  - headlights: Dave spent a lot of time cleaning, polishing, and protecting his headlights, which Calvin thought looked enchant